   "search_text": "Problem 3. We call a positive integer n peculiar  if, for any positive divisor d of n, the integer\nd(d + 1) divides n(n + 1). Prove that for any four different peculiar positive integers A, B, C and D,\nthe following holds:\n                                    gcd(A, B, C, D) = 1.\nHere gcd(A, B, C, D) is the largest positive integer that divides all of A, B, C and D.\n\n\n\n\n\nLanguage: English                                             Time: 4 hours and 30 minutes\n                                                        Each problem is worth 7 points\n",
